  "question": "Students in an introductory pedagogy course can reproduce course definitions but struggle to apply them to new classroom cases. Which redesign would most faithfully reflect constructivist learning theory?",
  "options": {
    "A": "Replace applications with additional lectures, note-taking templates, and memorization drills.",
    "B": "Present an authentic classroom dilemma, have teams investigate competing explanations, and provide instructor modeling, prompts, and feedback as groups construct and revise a proposed solution.",
