  "correct_answer": "B",
  "rationale": "The ZPD concerns capabilities that are emerging but not yet independently mastered. A skilled partner can support performance through contingent scaffolding, guidance, or encouragement, which is gradually internalized by the learner. Options A and C overlook guided performance, while D confines instruction to already mastered abilities."
}

