  "question": "During single-leg terminal stance, the ground-reaction force produces a 270 N·m dorsiflexion torque at the ankle. Neglecting angular acceleration, the Achilles tendon must generate an equal plantarflexion torque. Its perpendicular moment arm is 0.045 m, and its cross-sectional area is 0.90 cm². Which combination of tendon force and tensile stress is most accurate?",
  "options": {
