    "C": "13,500 N and 150 MPa",
    "D": "270 N and 3 MPa"
  },
  "correct_answer": "B",
  "rationale": "Using torque equilibrium, Achilles tendon force = 270 N·m ÷ 0.045 m = 6,000 N. The area of 0.90 cm² equals 90 mm², so tensile stress = 6,000 N ÷ 90 mm² = 66.7 N/mm², or 66.7 MPa."
}

