  "question": "A 67-year-old man presents with 2 hours of severe substernal chest pain and diaphoresis. His ECG shows dynamic ST-segment depression in V4–V6. High-sensitivity cardiac troponin T is initially below the 99th percentile but rises from 9 ng/L to 96 ng/L over 3 hours. What is the most appropriate diagnosis and immediate management?",
