    "stem": "A 62-year-old man presents 70 minutes after the onset of severe crushing chest pain. Electrocardiography demonstrates ST-segment elevation in leads II, III, aVF, and V4R, with reciprocal ST depression in leads I and aVL. His blood pressure is 82/54 mmHg. Examination reveals jugular venous distention and clear lung fields. What is the most appropriate immediate management while arranging reperfusion therapy?",
