      {
        "point": "Geometric interpretation",
        "explanation": "At a constrained extremum, the level curve f(x,y) = k and the constraint curve g(x,y) = c are tangent. Their normal vectors, ∇f and ∇g, are therefore parallel."
      },
      {
        "point": "Complete candidate system",
        "explanation": "For two variables, solve ∂f/∂x = λ∂g/∂x, ∂f/∂y = λ∂g/∂y, and g(x,y) = c simultaneously. The unknowns are x, y, and λ."
