        "The increment W_t − W_s is normally distributed with mean 0 and variance t − s.",
        "Disjoint increments are independent.",
        "W_t is almost surely continuous but nowhere differentiable.",
        "The process has quadratic variation [W]_t = t."
      ],
      "small_increment_approximation": "W_(t+Δt) − W_t ≈ √Δt Z, where Z has the standard normal distribution."
    },
    {
      "topic": "3. Standard scalar SDE",
      "equation": "dX_t = μ(X_t,t)dt + σ(X_t,t)dW_t",
      "integral_form": "X_t = X_0 + ∫₀ᵗ μ(X_s,s)ds + ∫₀ᵗ σ(X_s,s)dW_s",
      "interpretation": [
        "The drift integral describes cumulative systematic change.",
        "The stochastic integral describes cumulative random change.",
        "The parameter μ has units of state per unit time.",
        "The parameter σ has units of state per square-root time because W_t has units of square-root time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "4. Itô calculus",
      "ito_algebra": [
        "dt² is negligible to first order.",
        "dt dW is negligible to first order.",
        "The effective rule is (dW)² = dt."
      ],
      "ito_formula": "If X_t follows an Itô SDE and f is sufficiently smooth, then df = f_t dt + f_x dX_t + 0.5f_xx dt. After substituting dX_t, the coefficient of dt includes the second-order correction 0.5σ²f_xx."
    },
    {
      "topic": "5. Analytical solution patterns",
      "patterns": [
        "Additive-noise SDE with constant coefficients",
        "Linear SDE",
        "Geometric Brownian motion",
        "Ornstein–Uhlenbeck process as an extension"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "6. Numerical approximation",
      "method": "Euler–Maruyama",
      "equation": "X_(n+1) = X_n + μ(X_n,t_n)Δt + σ(X_n,t_n)ΔW_n, where ΔW_n = √Δt Z_n and Z_n is standard normal."
