      {
        "misconception": "Every subset of R is Lebesgue measurable.",
        "correction": "In the standard Lebesgue sigma-algebra, all subsets of null Borel sets are measurable, but not every subset of R is measurable. The construction of nonmeasurable sets shows that unrestricted measurability is impossible in the usual set-theoretic framework."
