        "explanation": "For an ideal-gas system at constant temperature, decreasing volume shifts equilibrium toward the side with fewer moles of gas. Increasing volume shifts it toward the side with more moles of gas. If the gas-mole totals are equal, there is no ideal-gas equilibrium shift."
