      "For either maximally entangled state, each reduced density matrix is I/2. Alice’s local measurement choice does not alter Bob’s reduced state when her result is not supplied. Conditioning on Alice’s result changes Bob’s conditional state, but using that condition requires communication.",
      "The detection loophole asks whether discarded or undetected events could hide nonlocal correlations. The locality loophole asks whether the measurement events are sufficiently space-like separated. Measurement independence is the assumption that hidden variables are independent of the chosen measurement settings.",
