        "point": "Integral control",
        "explanation": "The I term accumulates past errors and can eliminate steady-state error. Excessive integral action may cause overshoot, long settling time, and integral windup."
      },
      {
        "point": "Derivative control",
        "explanation": "The D term responds to the rate of change of error and can improve damping. It is sensitive to measurement noise and may produce a derivative kick."
      },
