        "Printed or digital Bode, Nyquist, and time-response plots"
      ]
    },
    "teaching_objectives": {
      "knowledge_and_understanding": [
        "Define robustness as stability and performance maintained over a specified family of plant models rather than at one nominal model.",
        "Distinguish model uncertainty, external disturbances, measurement noise, unmodeled dynamics, delays, and actuator constraints.",
        "Explain nominal stability, robust stability, robust performance, and internal stability.",
        "Interpret sensitivity and complementary-sensitivity transfer functions.",
        "Explain the H∞ norm as a worst-case frequency-domain amplification measure.",
        "Describe the basic ideas of small-gain analysis, structured uncertainty, and the structured singular value μ."
