    "Core_Thesis": "Stare decisis is a principle of judicial institutional restraint rather than a command to preserve every earlier result. A court generally follows the relevant holding of a superior court and, subject to local rules, its own prior decisions. It may depart for recognized reasons, but it should explain the departure and consider certainty, reliance, consistency, and the continuing quality of the precedent.",
    "Key_Points": [
