        "ID": "KP4",
        "Point": "Vertical and horizontal precedent",
        "Explanation": "Vertical stare decisis requires lower courts to follow controlling decisions of higher courts within the same jurisdictional hierarchy. Horizontal stare decisis concerns whether a court should follow decisions of the same court or another court at the same appellate level. Its strictness varies between systems."
