        "ID": "KP5",
        "Point": "Follow, distinguish, overrule, and reverse",
        "Explanation": "Following applies the precedent to a materially similar dispute. Distinguishing treats the earlier case as inapplicable because a material fact or legal issue differs, while leaving the precedent valid. Overruling declares an earlier holding no longer controlling. Reversing concerns the result of an appeal and does not necessarily mean that a precedent has been overruled."
      },
