      {
        "point": "Departure from precedent",
        "explanation": "In some common law systems, the highest court may depart from its own prior decisions in exceptional circumstances. The exact rule differs by jurisdiction and should always be verified."
      },
      {
        "point": "Distinguishing overruling from reversal",
        "explanation": "Reversing a decision means changing the result of a particular appeal. Overruling a decision changes the precedential status of the legal principle for future cases."
      },
