    "The classical beta-receptor pathway is beta receptor -> Gs protein -> adenylyl cyclase -> increased cAMP -> protein kinase A activation.",
    "Beta-1 blockade reduces heart rate, atrioventricular nodal conduction, myocardial contractility, and renin release from juxtaglomerular cells.",
    "Beta-2 blockade reduces beta-2-mediated smooth-muscle relaxation, especially in bronchial and vascular smooth muscle, and may cause bronchospasm and peripheral vasoconstriction.",
    "Beta-1 selectivity is relative and dose-dependent. Increasing the dose of a beta-1-selective drug can reduce selectivity and increase beta-2 blockade.",
    "Some beta-blockers have additional properties. Labetalol and carvedilol also block alpha-1 receptors, which adds vasodilatory effects."
