      "point": "Behavior is influenced by context",
      "explanation": "Time pressure, unclear criteria, emotionally charged situations, strong group identities, lack of accountability, and competing demands can make people more dependent on shortcuts."
    },
    {
      "point": "Bias operates at multiple levels",
      "explanation": "It appears in individual mental processes, interpersonal behavior, organizational decisions, institutional policies, and technological systems."
    },
    {
      "point": "Awareness is a starting point rather than a complete solution",
      "explanation": "Effective responses combine self-awareness with structured criteria, accountability, feedback, inclusive procedures, and institutional monitoring."
    },
    {
      "point": "Intersectionality matters",
      "explanation": "People hold multiple identities, and the relevance of an identity changes by situation. A person's gender, race, age, disability, religion, social class, or other characteristics may interact in complex ways."
