    "conceptual_summary": "Cognitive reappraisal is the deliberate interpretation of an emotionally meaningful event from a different, more flexible perspective. Its immediate effects involve cognitive control, contextual retrieval, and regulation of emotional and physiological responses. When reappraisal is practiced repeatedly, experience-dependent neuroplasticity may support longer-term changes in synaptic efficiency, functional connectivity, and possibly gray-matter structure. Acute regulatory activation should not, however, be confused with neuroplastic change, and positive reinterpretation should not replace realistic problem-solving or support-seeking.",
