        "topic": "Whole-of-society coordination",
        "explanation": "Cyber incidents may involve government agencies, military organizations, private-sector operators, critical infrastructure providers, civil society, and international partners. Effective coordination requires shared terminology, clear roles, information-sharing rules, and decision protocols.",
        "teaching_takeaway": "Cyber resilience is both a technical program and an institutional coordination challenge."
      }
    ],
    "difficulties": [
      {
        "difficulty": "Students conflate strategy, tactics, and techniques.",
        "common_error": "Calling a software patch, alert, or firewall rule a strategic decision.",
        "teaching_response": "Use a classification activity that asks teams to identify the desired end state, the coordination requirement, and the concrete method."
      },
