{
  "title": "Strategic Implications of Cyber Warfare",
  "module_type": "Lecture, discussion, and policy tabletop",
  "target_audience": "Upper-secondary or introductory university learners",
  "duration_minutes": 90,
  "module_overview": "This module examines how state and non-state actors use digital capabilities to influence security, politics, economics, and social stability. The focus is strategic rather than technical. Learners analyze escalation, deterrence, resilience, attribution, information operations, international law, alliances, and civilian protection. The term cyber warfare is treated as a contested label because not every cyber incident constitutes warfare or an armed attack.",
