      "task_1": "Slope = 3; y-intercept = -4. When x increases by 1, y increases by 3.",
      "task_2": "Slope = 8/6 = 4/3. A positive slope means the path rises as the horizontal distance increases.",
      "task_3": "f(1) = 1 and f(3) = 9, so the average rate of change is (9 - 1)/(3 - 1) = 8/2 = 4.",
      "task_4": "f(2) = 4. From 1.9 to 2.1, the average rate is (4.41 - 3.61)/(2.1 - 1.9) = 0.8/0.2 = 4. From 1.99 to 2.01, the result is approximately 4 as well. This stable value estimates the instantaneous rate of change at x = 2.",
      "task_5": "A line's slope is its constant rate of change. For a curved function, the instantaneous rate of change changes with x and can be estimated using slopes of very short secant lines."
    },
    "submission": [
      "Upload or sketch the graph and slope triangle.",
      "Show calculations for Tasks 3 and 4.",
      "Write the two- or three-sentence explanation for Task 5."
    ],
    "support_hint": "For Task 4, use the same average-rate-of-change formula from Task 3 and replace the endpoints with 1.9 and 2.1. Keep all decimal values aligned when subtracting.",
    "study_routine_note": "Complete this in one focused 25-minute session. If it is already late at night, use only Tasks 1, 3, and 5 for a 12-minute version and finish the rest after adequate sleep; attention and retention are strongest during a short daytime or early-evening session."
