    "why_the_three_cannot_all_be_guaranteed": "During a network partition, an isolated replica cannot determine whether another replica has accepted a newer update. It can reject requests until communication is restored, preserving consistency but sacrificing availability. Alternatively, it can continue serving requests, preserving availability but potentially returning stale data or accepting conflicting updates. Partition tolerance is generally not optional for a distributed system because network partitions cannot be completely prevented.",
