      "Use checklists, reframing, feedback, or environmental safeguards when the decision is consequential.",
      "Treat the two modes as interacting explanations rather than rigid categories."
    ],
    "conclusion": "Dual process theory implies that human decisions emerge from an interaction between rapid intuition and slower analysis. Its main value is to explain why efficiency, emotion, expertise, bias, and bounded information can all shape behavior, while also highlighting when deliberate intervention is needed."
  }
}

