  "proof": {
    "step_1": "Evaluate the function at x = 2: f(2) = 2^3 - 3(2) + 1 = 3.",
    "step_2": "For any ε > 0, we need a δ > 0 such that |x - 2| < δ implies |f(x) - f(2)| < ε.",
    "step_3": "Factor the difference: f(x) - f(2) = x^3 - 3x - 2 = (x - 2)(x + 1)^2.",
