    "step_5": "Thus, |f(x) - f(2)| = |x - 2||x + 1|^2 < δ · 16 ≤ ε."
  },
  "conclusion": "Therefore, for every ε > 0 there exists δ > 0 such that |x - 2| < δ implies |f(x) - f(2)| < ε. Hence f(x) = x^3 - 3x + 1 is continuous at x = 2."
